WEBVTT

00:01:57.442 --> 00:02:01.038
We're expected to be constantly
productive and creative

00:02:01.062 --> 00:02:02.577
in equal measure.

00:02:02.601 --> 00:02:04.318
But it's actually almost impossible

00:02:04.342 --> 00:02:06.798
for our brains to continuously
generate new ideas

00:02:06.822 --> 00:02:08.078
with no rest.

00:02:08.102 --> 00:02:11.808
In fact, downtime
is a necessity for our brain

00:02:11.832 --> 00:02:14.028
to recover and to operate properly.

00:02:14.052 --> 00:02:16.368
Consider that according
to a team of researchers

00:02:16.392 --> 00:02:18.728
from the University
of Southern California,

00:02:18.752 --> 00:02:22.138
letting our minds wander
is an essential mental state

00:02:22.162 --> 00:02:24.419
that helps us develop our identity,

00:02:24.443 --> 00:02:26.338
process social interactions,

00:02:26.362 --> 00:02:29.978
and it even influences
our internal moral compass.